   "source": [
    "## Q1: Sensor Readings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "747ec4c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "temperature = np.array([25, 28, 31, 35, 38, 27, 33, 40])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8fd0bfdb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a. Add 2°C to every reading using vectorization**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4ef21c52",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "corrected_temperature = temperature + 2\n",
    "print(corrected_temperature)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3f9ed490",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b. Convert corrected temperatures from Celsius to Fahrenheit**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "da483888",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fahrenheit = corrected_temperature * 9 / 5 + 32\n",
    "print(fahrenheit)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "669e4e91",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c. Identify all readings greater than 32°C using Boolean indexing**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "06f6de63",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "above_32 = corrected_temperature[corrected_temperature > 32]\n",
    "print(above_32)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7aedfa86",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**d. Count how many readings exceed 32°C**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a1ceeacd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "count_above_32 = np.sum(corrected_temperature > 32)\n",
    "print(count_above_32)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b2067ce5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**e. Explanation**\n",
    "\n",
    "Vectorization lets NumPy apply an operation to an entire array in a single, compiled, low-level loop written in C, instead of Python looping element by element. This avoids the overhead of Python's interpreter (type checking, function calls) on every single element, so operations run much faster and the code is shorter and easier to read.\n",
    "\n",
    "Boolean indexing works the same way: a condition like `corrected_temperature > 32` is evaluated across the whole array at once, producing a Boolean mask, which is then used to select matching elements directly. This is far more efficient than writing an explicit for loop with an `if` check for every value, especially as the dataset grows large, since NumPy operations are executed in optimized, pre-compiled code rather than interpreted Python."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "31c980b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2: Daily Steps Matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eaf6be85",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "steps = np.array([\n",
    "    [5000, 6200, 7100],\n",
    "    [8000, 7500, 9000],\n",
    "    [4500, 5100, 4800],\n",
    "    [9000, 8500, 9500]\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "321fcc3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a. Total steps recorded**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ba901632",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_steps = steps.sum()\n",
    "print(total_steps)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "32c44f0d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b. Mean number of steps**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b4154d39",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mean_steps = steps.mean()\n",
    "print(mean_steps)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b6ab3b54",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c. Maximum and minimum values**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "92390d4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "max_steps = steps.max()\n",
    "min_steps = steps.min()\n",
    "print(max_steps, min_steps)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8790fab8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**d. Total steps for each day (axis=0)**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "739322f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_per_day = steps.sum(axis=0)\n",
    "print(total_per_day)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91e03e4f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**e. Total steps for each user (axis=1)**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "28f41b70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "total_per_user = steps.sum(axis=1)\n",
    "print(total_per_user)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e9c11a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**f. User/day position with the maximum number of steps**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bcb4c7e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "max_index = np.argmax(steps)\n",
    "max_position = np.unravel_index(max_index, steps.shape)\n",
    "print(max_position)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9bb6d161",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3: Array Slicing, Views and Copies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7274cb01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a. Create the array**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "10709d52",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "original = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])\n",
    "print(original)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fd2d0134",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b. Slice from index 1 to 4**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "89befbbd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "subset = original[1:5]\n",
    "print(subset)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "154c904f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c. Modify first element of subset**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e8206643",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "subset[0] = 999\n",
    "print(\"original:\", original)\n",
    "print(\"subset:\", subset)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "08521906",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**d. Slice with .copy()**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ddaf7c91",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "original = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])\n",
    "subset_copy = original[1:5].copy()\n",
    "subset_copy[0] = 500\n",
    "print(\"original:\", original)\n",
    "print(\"subset_copy:\", subset_copy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb9ec9e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**e. Create 1–12 array and reshape into 3x4**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1f4056ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "matrix = np.arange(1, 13).reshape(3, 4)\n",
    "print(matrix)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "170a73ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**f. Indexing and slicing the 3x4 matrix**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "4b563a04",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "first_row = matrix[0]\n",
    "last_row = matrix[-1]\n",
    "second_column = matrix[:, 1]\n",
    "sub_matrix = matrix[0:2, 1:3]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"first row:\", first_row)\n",
    "print(\"last row:\", last_row)\n",
    "print(\"second column:\", second_column)\n",
    "print(\"sub matrix:\\n\", sub_matrix)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "69c5193f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**g. Flatten the matrix using flatten() and ravel()**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fc0332ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "flattened = matrix.flatten()\n",
    "raveled = matrix.ravel()\n",
    "print(flattened)\n",
    "print(raveled)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "38c381da",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**h. Modify an element in the ravel() array**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "46e5e35f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "raveled[0] = 999\n",
    "print(\"matrix:\\n\", matrix)\n",
    "print(\"raveled:\", raveled)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b79ee168",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`ravel()` returns a view of the original array whenever possible, so changing an element in `raveled` also changes `matrix`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a9f8fcd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**i. Modify an element in the flatten() array**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "22aa5e6f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "flattened[0] = 888\n",
    "print(\"matrix:\\n\", matrix)\n",
    "print(\"flattened:\", flattened)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4b705a64",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`flatten()` always returns a copy of the data, so changing an element in `flattened` does not affect `matrix`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fc1508d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**j. Shape, ndim, size and dtype of the 3x4 matrix**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "94c9f74f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"shape:\", matrix.shape)\n",
    "print(\"ndim:\", matrix.ndim)\n",
    "print(\"size:\", matrix.size)\n",
    "print(\"dtype:\", matrix.dtype)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "63a41a13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4: Predicting Assistance Score"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "166467a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = np.array([\n",
    "    [6, 70, 3],\n",
    "    [5, 50, 6],\n",
    "    [8, 80, 2],\n",
    "    [4, 30, 8]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "y = np.array([40, 65, 30, 85])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4fd3bdf2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**a. Shape and dimensions of X**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "17879525",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"shape:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(\"ndim:\", X.ndim)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab46d95c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**b. Transpose of X**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "05da28cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_T = X.T\n",
    "print(X_T)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6d0e8eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`X.T` swaps rows and columns: each of the 3 original features (sleep hours, activity level, stress level) becomes a row instead of a column, and each user becomes a column instead of a row. This reoriented layout is what makes matrix operations like `X.T @ X` and `X.T @ y` valid, since it aligns the feature dimension for matrix multiplication."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f78f0d42",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**c. Matrix product X.T @ X**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e8eacaf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "XtX = X.T @ X\n",
    "print(XtX)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "90936be4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**d. Matrix inverse of X.T @ X**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b375083c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "XtX_inv = np.linalg.inv(XtX)\n",
    "print(XtX_inv)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ff3acf02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**e. Ordinary Least Squares coefficients**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "35b88b45",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "beta = np.linalg.inv(X.T @ X) @ X.T @ y\n",
    "print(beta)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce8c4b61",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**f. What the coefficients represent**\n",
    "\n",
    "Each value in `beta` is the weight assigned to one of the three features (sleep hours, activity level, stress level) in a linear model that predicts the assistance score. A coefficient tells us how much the predicted assistance score changes for a one-unit increase in that feature, assuming the other two features stay constant. A positive coefficient (e.g. for sleep hours or activity level) means the assistance score tends to rise as that feature increases, while a negative coefficient (e.g. for stress level) means the score tends to fall as that feature increases. The relative magnitude of each coefficient also indicates how strongly that feature drives the prediction compared to the others, within this small dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a17a53ec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**g. Predicting the assistance score for a new user**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "12572909",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "new_user = np.array([6, 65, 4])\n",
    "predicted_score = new_user @ beta\n",
    "print(predicted_score)"
   ]
  }
